\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-180\li180\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Make me more vibrant.  O my Lord,\cf0 
\par \pard\li180\sl190\slmult0 In both my life and death
\par Grant that I truly slow thee Love
\par :/: With all the strength I have. :/:
\par 
\par \pard\fi-180\li180\sl190\slmult0\qj\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Grant me your favours, my good Lord
\par \pard\li180\sl190\slmult0 That your face I may see.
\par If worship here on earth's pleasant,
\par :/: How will it be above? :/:
\par 
\par \pard\fi-180\li270\sl190\slmult0\qj\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Troubles and thoughts shall have an end,
\par \pard\li270\sl190\slmult0 so shall bad days to end;
\par We shall unite with all the saints
\par :/: And sing Hallelujah! :/:\tab 
\par 
\par \pard\fi-180\li270\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Of life above we do not know,
\par \pard\li270\sl190\slmult0\qj Invisible it is though.
\par because of what the Lord Christ said,
\par :/: We'll always stay with Him. :/:
\par \pard\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2\fs14 
\par }

